                     {
                         "version":  "2026.11.1111",
                         "date":  "2026-11-11",
                         "channel":  "beta",
                         "important":  true,
                         "notes":  "### Added\r\n- Research → Perioperative Table: **P-values in a stratified table**: across the whole cohort (as before, the default), within each stratum (a P-value column per stratum), or both\r\n- Research → Perioperative Table: **Show which test** adds a Test column naming each row\u0027s test\r\n- Research → Perioperative Table: **Welch\u0027s test for mean ± SD** (off by default, to keep matching R\u0027s tableone) tests mean ± SD rows without assuming equal spreads\r\n- Research → Perioperative Table: **Show SMD** adds a standardised mean difference column for two-group tables, as R\u0027s tableone computes it\r\n- Research → Perioperative Table: date fields can be added: they show the median date with the first and third quartile dates, and their p-value uses the Kruskal-Wallis test\r\n\r\n### Fixed\r\n- Research → Perioperative Table: in a stratified table, the group counts in brackets in **N (non-missing)** were each group\u0027s number of records, not the number with a value for the field (an unstratified table was right). **Regenerate stratified tables to correct them**; no other numbers change",
